{"title":"2018 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_ANALYSIS!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE ANALYSIS!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Meta-Solving_Technique)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Meta-Solving Technique)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8dcf98ed1b21dbc446aa28d097d4281599c25e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/24096979a27c72ccde79e7e4889bf4e4be7a632b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92c20bfa6b6c6f932df6dd6a9f0b2c881179e70b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB=2.$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" /> Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/6/bf625d97558cbdc51ab8fef465b17fddf270d3d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE} \\parallel \\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851fd6c90b73b80bb0e0fd2cc7fa51aaf4e11ec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{EF} \\parallel \\overline{AC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" /> What is the ratio of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/28283830381a9931fc4e44deac6f63dc43a61889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> to the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93a9ae954a85d68fcab8e16b65857097f814792b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC?$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/7/0571cfd5e8f21ce8031af38df8ba2295bdf2449a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(7cm); pair A,B,C,DD,EE,FF; A = (0,0); B = (3,0); C = (0.5,2.5); EE = (1,0); DD = intersectionpoint(A--C,EE--EE+(C-B)); FF = intersectionpoint(B--C,EE--EE+(C-A)); draw(A--B--C--A--DD--EE--FF,black+1bp); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,DD,W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,EE,S); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,FF,NE); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(A+EE)/2,S); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(EE+B)/2,S); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"305\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e45516f9a72e1edf35064c4cddcd58645cfafad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{4}{9} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{5}{9} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{3}{5} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"371\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By similar triangles, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/8/b48db370dc7aea2d659840124dfae3d8666c6c87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADE] = \\frac{1}{9}[ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"142\" height=\"37\" />. Similarly, we see that [mathjax][BEF] = \\dfrac{4}{9}[ABC][/mathjax]. Using this information, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67cde5e80fcc5b626eb89dddebf3a68bd64c8405.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ACFE] = \\frac{5}{9}[ABC].\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"37\" /> Then, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/8/b48db370dc7aea2d659840124dfae3d8666c6c87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADE] = \\frac{1}{9}[ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"142\" height=\"37\" />, it follows that the [mathjax][CDEF] = \\dfrac{4}{9}[ABC][/mathjax]. Thus, the answer would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/6187ab3d75075f143eaaee14be9c359718f9743c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{4}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"60\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Sidenote: [mathjax][ABC][/mathjax] denotes the area of triangle [mathjax]ABC[/mathjax]. Similarly, [mathjax][ABCD][/mathjax] denotes the area of figure [mathjax]ABCD[/mathjax].\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c7184561716c81ff7a733d6d1356c9d58e26a61b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c42fa443adbef221d28478ebe392db1a4cf44b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b =$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. We can extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> to form a parallelogram, which would equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/8/3f89bd1e25435bfeb07be0298db571e6904adf39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a \\cdot 3b$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. The smaller parallelogram is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> times <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b30259d95f64f9aa7c6bd36e1583618a23c8bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />. The smaller parallelogram is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041a0b37ca609642fb34c7c855b9d67ed498a560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the larger parallelogram, so the answer would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fac8fdd6ce131c3cdfda44bbc276a3fa380756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{9} \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"37\" height=\"38\" />, since the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the parallelogram, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/6187ab3d75075f143eaaee14be9c359718f9743c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{4}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"60\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>By babyzombievillager with credits to many others who helped with the solution :D\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea360545652d276e392a5c7e3f38f5bf9d0514e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ADE} \\sim \\triangle{ABC} \\sim \\triangle{EFB}$\" width=\"226\" height=\"13\" />. We can substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b6691251a362837413262d094d29f92be951d579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da1bb9c169ddba5c7fe4473d8780c7402eff24b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3c4c37c5debae414b63672cc9607bbc8273a001.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/a/84ae51dd95ca59139201d0895df8311e612782fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> having, distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> parts also. And, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc7f4fd0e5897e8ac812a9a562556b8cdd87341f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CF}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56a5efb54b46587c420e1101dc0ef393707a28d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{FB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85764febdaf339469a545d7e698ddf7ad57ea9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"22\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd665aa740b89dbf22d9030c5fb511b39ef0b9f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"22\" height=\"37\" /> respectfully. You can consider the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/acad5629f89ba033c79d7d59d7c0605d2a5cac48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ADE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2a1d949aefc17f58ae1107c42ac24aa99dec30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EFB}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/612cb53032b6b7359a67ad3d622a6b2208728afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2z$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> respectfully. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/acad5629f89ba033c79d7d59d7c0605d2a5cac48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ADE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cda74d11208942f7069de7220efe06c43d6162f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1\\cdot z}{2}=0.5z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"91\" height=\"37\" /> because the area formula for a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/ddd1952ffb713991003b4c82e0150177396b8271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}bh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"31\" height=\"37\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/e/2ce4b902246a68e80a0f0417d8072f96cde6fb0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{bh}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"39\" />. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2a1d949aefc17f58ae1107c42ac24aa99dec30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{EFB}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/f/6dfd06dab420c4ee4a05132dc5008c9c2e3389e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2\\cdot 2z}{2}=2z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"86\" height=\"37\" />. So, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cab1dbe495c410bfd386e200d00a1589885d2edf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3\\cdot (2z+z)}{2}=\\frac{3\\cdot 3z}{2}=\\frac{9z}{2}=4.5z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"261\" height=\"38\" />. The area of parallelogram <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/28283830381a9931fc4e44deac6f63dc43a61889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df27ad0b48ef24ae536eb0cf846eb4af9db99ed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.5z-(0.5z+2z)=4.5z-2.5z=2z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"298\" height=\"20\" />. Parallelogram <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/28283830381a9931fc4e44deac6f63dc43a61889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bfaecfb943ba9e21d219504e2bb11b122ef1178.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}= \\frac{2z}{4.5z}=\\frac{2}{4.5}=\\frac{4}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"206\" height=\"37\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/6187ab3d75075f143eaaee14be9c359718f9743c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{4}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"60\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_ANALYSIS.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_ANALYSIS!!!)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE ANALYSIS!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE ANALYSIS!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ayUmpmgFi3E\">https://youtu.be/ayUmpmgFi3E</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Meta-Solving_Technique.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Meta-Solving_Technique)\">Video Solution (Meta-Solving Technique)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Meta-Solving Technique)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GmUWIXXf_uk?t=1541\">https://youtu.be/GmUWIXXf_uk?t=1541</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/V_-yIhs_Bps\">https://youtu.be/V_-yIhs_Bps</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TpsuRedYOiM&amp;t=250s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TpsuRedYOiM&amp;t=250s</a>\n(by SpreadTheMathLove)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 8\">2018 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2018\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\